          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "टक्का (ṭakkā) is usually traced to Sanskrit ṭaṅka, \"a stamped coin\", under which CDIAL lists Marathi ṭakā, \"a two-paisa coin\" (CDIAL 5426); the sense one in a hundred came later, and Gujarati ṭako has it too."
            }
